.TH PINENTRY-DMENU 1 "DATE" pinentry-dmenu\-VERSION "pinentry-dmenu Manual"


.SH NAME
pinentry-dmenu - a pinentry program with the charm of dmenu
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pinentry-dmenu 
is a dmenu- and pinentry-based passphrase dialog called from the
.BR gpg-agent (1)
daemon. It is not intended to be invoked directly.


.SH SYNOPSIS
Set the 
.B pinentry-program
in
.IR ~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf
to
.B pinentry-dmenu
to use the program as the regular dialog for
.BR gpg-agent .
.PP
The configuration is placed in
.IR ~/.gnupg/pinentry-dmenu.conf .
You can change the path to the config file with the environment variable
.IR GNUPGHOME .


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "asterisk =" " *"
Defines the symbol which is showed for each typed character.
.TP
.BI "horizontal_padding =" " 20"
Horizontal padding around text.
.TP
.BI "lines =" " 8"
Number of reserved description rows. Longer descriptions expand the window.
.TP
.BI "monitor =" " -1"
pinentry-dmenu is displayed on the monitor number supplied. Monitor numbers are starting from 0.
.TP
.BI "prompt =" " """"
Defines the prompt to be displayed to the left of the input field.
.TP
.BI "font =" " monospace:size=10"
Defines the font or font set used.
.TP
.BI "prompt_bg =" " #bbbbbb"
Defines the prompt background color.
.IR #RGB ,
.I #RRGGBB
and X color names are supported.
.TP
.BI "prompt_fg =" " #222222"
Defines the prompt foreground color.
.TP
.BI "normal_bg =" " #bbbbbb"
Defines the normal background color.
.TP
.BI "normal_fg =" " #222222"
Defines the normal foreground color.
.TP
.BI "select_bg =" " #eeeeee"
Defines the selected background color.
.TP
.BI "select_fg =" " #005577"
Defines the selected foreground color.
.TP
.BI "desc_bg =" " #bbbbbb"
Defines the description background color.
.TP
.BI "desc_fg =" " #222222"
Defines the description foreground color.
.TP
.BI "error_bg =" " #cc3333"
Defines the error background color.
.TP
.BI "error_fg =" " #ffffff"
Defines the error foreground color.
.TP
.BI "embedded =" " false"
Embed into window.


.SH USAGE
pinentry-dmenu is completely controlled by the keyboard.
.TP
.B Return
Confirm input
.TP
.B Ctrl-Return
Confirm input
.TP
.B Shift\-Return
Confirm input
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel input
.TP
.B C\-c
Escape

.SS Confirm Mode
.TP
.B Left / Right
Select an action. Move mouse over action row to select it.
.TP
.B Return
Activate selected action.
.TP
.B Left mouse button
Activate action row. In pin mode, clear input line.
.TP
.B Middle mouse button
Paste primary selection in pin mode.
.TP
.B Right mouse button
Cancel request.
.TP
.B g
Cancel input
.TP
.B G
Cancel input
.TP
.B n
Select the not-ok action.
.TP
.B N
Select the not-ok action.
.TP
.B y
Select the ok action.
.TP
.B Y
Select the ok action.

.SS Pin Mode
.TP
.B End
Move cursor to the line end
.TP
.B Home
Move cursor to the line begin
.TP
.B C\-a
Home
.TP
.B C\-b
Left
.TP
.B C\-d
Delete
.TP
.B C\-e
End
.TP
.B C\-f
Right
.TP
.B C\-g
Escape
.TP
.B C\-h
Backspace
.TP
.B C\-k
Delete line right
.TP
.B C\-u
Delete line left
.TP
.B C\-v
Paste from primary X selection


.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
.if n \{
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
asterisk= "# ";
prompt = "$";
font = "Noto Sans UI:size=13";
prompt_fg = "#eeeeee";
prompt_bg = "#d9904a";
normal_fg = "#ffffff";
normal_bg = "#000000";
select_fg = "#eeeeee";
select_bg = "#d9904a";
desc_fg = "#eeeeee";
desc_bg = "#d9904a";


